// uk-gdpr — UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018
//
// The law: personal data may leave the UK only for a country covered by
// UK adequacy regulations or under appropriate safeguards (the IDTA or the
// UK Addendum to the EU clauses).
//
// This pack: everything runs in the UK or a country with UK adequacy, on
// offers with a contract and an audit (T2 or better).
//
// Not covered: transfers under the IDTA or the Addendum, and the UK
// Extension to the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, which covers only
// certified US organisations.
//
// Use `import "uk-gdpr"`. Not legal advice.

policy uk-gdpr {
  residency = uk-adequate
  min_trust = T2
}
